      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: prevent parallel talk tests from sharing SQLite state",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where parallel OpenClaw checkouts on the same machine could share the real `/tmp/openclaw-agent.sqlite` database while running `src/talk/agent-consult-runtime.test.ts`. A newer checkout could advance that database to schema version 11, causing an older checkout that supports schema version 10 to fail.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nEach test now gets a `realpath`-canonicalized `mkdtemp` directory, and every mocked agent, workspace, session, and store path derives from it. Teardown closes the exact cached agent database before recursively removing the directory. A sibling-test scan found no other hardcoded `/tmp` paths under `src/talk`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo runtime behavior changes. Maintainers and contributors can run talk tests from parallel worktrees without cross-checkout SQLite schema contamination.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/talk` — 37 files passed, 219 tests passed on the final rebased head.\n- `node scripts/check-changed.mjs` — core test typecheck, changed-file lint, formatting, temp-directory guard, and boundary checks passed on [Blacksmith Testbox](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29595365269).\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode uncommitted` — clean; no accepted or actionable findings.\n- `rg` scan — no hardcoded `/tmp` paths remain in `src/talk` test/spec files.\n\nAI-assisted with Codex. I reviewed the implementation and validation results.\n",
